00:26:05.140 --> 00:26:07.510
I'm no different than
when I left here.

482
00:26:07.510 --> 00:26:11.890
[gasps]
You're showing
gratitude to others?

483
00:26:11.890 --> 00:26:14.190
You don't need to be scared!

484
00:26:15.560 --> 00:26:17.060
[laughs]

485
00:26:18.360 --> 00:26:20.480
[laughs]

486
00:26:20.480 --> 00:26:22.110
[NARRATOR]
Oden rushed to the capital

487
00:26:22.110 --> 00:26:24.200
when he heard that
his father had fallen ill,

488
00:26:24.200 --> 00:26:27.780
but seeing his son again seemed
to invigorate the shogun.

489
00:26:27.780 --> 00:26:30.490
However, this is the last time

490
00:26:30.490 --> 00:26:34.080
that the two would
exchange words.

491
00:26:34.460 --> 00:26:36.580
[Whitebeard Pirates chattering]

492
00:26:36.580 --> 00:26:38.920
[WHITEBEARD PIRATE A]
Seems
people live on this island.

493
00:26:38.920 --> 00:26:40.040
[WHITEBEARD PIRATE B]
Pops, it's gonna take

494
00:26:40.040 --> 00:26:42.340
at least a week
to patch this up.

495
00:26:42.960 --> 00:26:45.300
[WHITEY BAY]
The water ruined all our cargo.

496
00:26:44.040 --> 00:26:48.670
<b>The Same Year


Itachi Port

Kuri</b>

497
00:26:45.300 --> 00:26:48.220
[RAKUYO]
First off, we need
to get food and supplies.

498
00:26:48.220 --> 00:26:49.760
Who wants to go?

499
00:26:49.760 --> 00:26:51.350
Most of us, probably.

500
00:26:51.350 --> 00:26:53.430
We all gotta stretch
our legs, don't we?

501
00:26:55.350 --> 00:26:57.270
No way. You're still
just a deckhand.

502
00:26:56.680 --> 00:27:00.310
<b>Captain Edward Newgate


Whitebeard Pirates</b>

503
00:26:57.270 --> 00:27:00.230
We just climbed up a waterfall.

504
00:27:02.280 --> 00:27:03.320
Yet there's sea here,
and an island, somehow.

505
00:27:03.320 --> 00:27:07.160
[Whitebeard]
Yet there's sea
here, and an island, somehow.

506
00:27:08.130 --> 00:27:09.220
[villagers gasp]

507
00:27:13.010 --> 00:27:15.640
Trouble, sir! We need
your help, quick!

508
00:27:16.970 --> 00:27:20.730
What is it? Calm yourself.
You're too loud!

509
00:27:20.730 --> 00:27:23.560
There's giant pirate ship
docked at Itachi Port!

510
00:27:23.560 --> 00:27:26.190
[gasps]
A pirate ship?

511
00:27:26.190 --> 00:27:27.570
[subordinate A gasps]

512
00:27:27.570 --> 00:27:29.440
[chuckles]

513
00:27:29.440 --> 00:27:33.570
[gasps]
Lord Oden!
Where are you going?

514
00:27:33.570 --> 00:27:35.490
To the port!

515
00:27:36.740 --> 00:27:38.740
Go, go, go!

516
00:27:40.540 --> 00:27:43.330
All right, then,
we'll go get food and supplies!

517
00:27:43.330 --> 00:27:45.080
And I'll come with you!

518
00:27:45.080 --> 00:27:48.170
No way. I told you,
no deckhands allowed.

519
00:27:48.170 --> 00:27:49.880
Aw, don't be like that!

520
00:27:49.880 --> 00:27:52.510
Hey, Pops. I can go with
the crew, right?

521
00:27:52.510 --> 00:27:54.220
Do what you want.

522
00:27:54.220 --> 00:27:57.760
[Marco chuckles]
You heard him! Off we go!

523
00:27:57.760 --> 00:28:01.310
[Whitey Bay]
Yeah, and you
heard me say "no"! Now, stay!

524
00:28:01.310 --> 00:28:05.940
Wait, what? Lord Oden
ran off to the port?

525
00:28:05.940 --> 00:28:07.820
Why did you let him go?

526
00:28:07.820 --> 00:28:09.900
I heard a pirate ship
showed up outta nowhere!

527
00:28:09.900 --> 00:28:11.360
They say it looks real crazy!

528
00:28:11.360 --> 00:28:14.070
It's bigger than our ships
and the pirates look tough!

529
00:28:14.070 --> 00:28:15.570
Stop him at any cost!

530
00:28:15.570 --> 00:28:18.240
Surely he's just going there
to chase the pirates away!

531
00:28:18.240 --> 00:28:19.410
Not a chance!

532
00:28:19.410 --> 00:28:21.910
You know that this is
his dream, right?

533
00:28:21.910 --> 00:28:24.750
He wants to set sail!

534
00:28:24.750 --> 00:28:27.210
[laughs]

535
00:28:28.130 --> 00:28:31.260
[Oden]
That must be it!
The pirate ship!

536
00:28:31.260 --> 00:28:36.470
Finally! Freedom!

537
00:28:36.470 --> 00:28:40.100
[gasps]
We're in trouble.

538
00:28:41.060 --> 00:28:43.140
[Whitebeard]
All of you need to stand back.

539
00:28:43.140 --> 00:28:44.390
Huh?

540
00:28:44.390 --> 00:28:46.400
Someone's coming for us!

541
00:28:46.400 --> 00:28:48.820
Someone extraordinary.

542
00:28:48.820 --> 00:28:50.650
Glad you could make it!

543
00:28:50.650 --> 00:28:53.280
Braving the storms,
climbing the waterfall.

544
00:28:53.280 --> 00:28:55.990
We don't get many visitors here!

545
00:28:59.200 --> 00:29:01.410
[grunts]

546
00:29:06.000 --> 00:29:07.580
[grunts]

547
00:29:40.600 --> 00:29:43.930
I'll teach you
a thing or two, boy!

548
00:29:47.980 --> 00:29:49.560
[Oden grunts]

549
00:29:53.990 --> 00:29:57.110
[Oden grunts]

550
00:29:58.950 --> 00:30:00.740
[grunts]

551
00:30:00.740 --> 00:30:02.910
[Whitebeard grunts]

552
00:30:12.630 --> 00:30:16.470
I've been waiting for
someone like you, pirate!

553
00:30:16.470 --> 00:30:18.680
My name is Kozuki Oden!

554
00:30:18.680 --> 00:30:21.970
I don't know who you are,
but you're my ticket out!

555
00:30:21.970 --> 00:30:23.560
Take me with you!
